#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:1
msgid "react-dev-utils"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This package includes some utilities used by [Create React "
"App](https://github.com/facebook/create-react-app).<br> Please refer to "
"its documentation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:6
msgid ""
"[Getting Started](https://facebook.github.io/create-react-app/docs"
"/getting-started) – How to create a new app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:7
msgid ""
"[User Guide](https://facebook.github.io/create-react-app/) – How to "
"develop apps bootstrapped with Create React App."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:9
msgid "Usage in Create React App Projects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:11
msgid ""
"These utilities come by default with [Create React "
"App](https://github.com/facebook/create-react-app). **You don’t need to "
"install it separately in Create React App projects.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:13
msgid "Usage Outside of Create React App"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:15
msgid ""
"If you don’t use Create React App, or if you "
"[ejected](https://facebook.github.io/create-react-app/docs/available-"
"scripts#npm-run-eject), you may keep using these utilities. Their "
"development will be aligned with Create React App, so major versions of "
"these utilities may come out relatively often. Feel free to fork or copy "
"and paste them into your projects if you’d like to have more control over"
" them, or feel free to use the old versions. Not all of them are React-"
"specific, but we might make some of them more React-specific in the "
"future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:17
msgid "Entry Points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:19
msgid ""
"There is no single entry point. You can only import individual top-level "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:21
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`new InterpolateHtmlPlugin(htmlWebpackPlugin: HtmlWebpackPlugin, "
"replacements: {[key:string]: string})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:23
msgid ""
"This webpack plugin lets us interpolate custom variables into "
"`index.html`.<br> It works in tandem with "
"[HtmlWebpackPlugin](https://github.com/ampedandwired/html-webpack-plugin)"
" 2.x via its [events](https://github.com/ampedandwired/html-webpack-"
"plugin#events)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:59
msgid ""
"`new InlineChunkHtmlPlugin(htmlWebpackPlugin: HtmlWebpackPlugin, tests: "
"Regex[])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:61
msgid ""
"This webpack plugin inlines script chunks into `index.html`.<br> It works"
" in tandem with [HtmlWebpackPlugin](https://github.com/ampedandwired"
"/html-webpack-plugin) 4.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:92
msgid ""
"`new ModuleScopePlugin(appSrc: string | string[], allowedFiles?: "
"string[])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:94
msgid ""
"This webpack plugin ensures that relative imports from app's source "
"directories don't reach outside of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:114
msgid "`new WatchMissingNodeModulesPlugin(nodeModulesPath: string)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:116
msgid ""
"This webpack plugin ensures `npm install <library>` forces a project "
"rebuild.<br> We’re not sure why this isn't webpack's default "
"behavior.<br> See [#186](https://github.com/facebook/create-react-"
"app/issues/186) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:139
msgid "`checkRequiredFiles(files: Array<string>): boolean`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:141
msgid ""
"Makes sure that all passed files exist.<br> Filenames are expected to be "
"absolute.<br> If a file is not found, prints a warning message and "
"returns `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:159
msgid "`clearConsole(): void`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:161
msgid "Clears the console, hopefully in a cross-platform way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:170
msgid "`eslintFormatter(results: Object): string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:172
msgid ""
"This is our custom ESLint formatter that integrates well with Create "
"React App console output.<br> You can use the default one instead if you "
"prefer so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:200
msgid "`FileSizeReporter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:202
msgid ""
"`measureFileSizesBeforeBuild(buildFolder: string): "
"Promise<OpaqueFileSizes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:204
msgid ""
"Captures JS and CSS asset sizes inside the passed `buildFolder`. Save the"
" result value to compare it after the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:206
msgid ""
"`printFileSizesAfterBuild(webpackStats: WebpackStats, previousFileSizes: "
"OpaqueFileSizes, buildFolder: string, maxBundleGzipSize?: number, "
"maxChunkGzipSize?: number)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:208
msgid ""
"Prints the JS and CSS asset sizes after the build, and includes a size "
"comparison with `previousFileSizes` that were captured earlier using "
"`measureFileSizesBeforeBuild()`. `maxBundleGzipSize` and "
"`maxChunkGzipSizemay` may optionally be specified to display a warning "
"when the main bundle or a chunk exceeds the specified size (in bytes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:223
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`formatWebpackMessages({errors: Array<string>, warnings: Array<string>}):"
" {errors: Array<string>, warnings: Array<string>}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:225
msgid ""
"Extracts and prettifies warning and error messages from webpack "
"[stats](https://github.com/webpack/docs/wiki/node.js-api#stats) object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:256
msgid "`printBuildError(error: Object): void`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:258
msgid ""
"Prettify some known build errors. Pass an Error object to log a "
"prettified error message in the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:270
msgid "`getProcessForPort(port: number): string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:272
msgid ""
"Finds the currently running process on `port`. Returns a string "
"containing the name and directory, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:286
msgid "`launchEditor(fileName: string, lineNumber: number): void`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:288
msgid ""
"On macOS, tries to find a known running editor process and opens the file"
" in it. It can also be explicitly configured by `REACT_EDITOR`, `VISUAL`,"
" or `EDITOR` environment variables. For example, you can put "
"`REACT_EDITOR=atom` in your `.env.local` file, and Create React App will "
"respect that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:290
msgid "`noopServiceWorkerMiddleware(servedPath: string): ExpressMiddleware`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:292
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Returns Express middleware that serves a `${servedPath}/service-"
"worker.js` that resets any previously set service worker configuration. "
"Useful for development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:294
msgid "`redirectServedPathMiddleware(servedPath: string): ExpressMiddleware`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:296
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Returns Express middleware that redirects to `${servedPath}/${req.path}`,"
" if `req.url` does not start with `servedPath`. Useful for development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:299
msgid "`openBrowser(url: string): boolean`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:301
msgid ""
"Attempts to open the browser with a given URL.<br> On Mac OS X, attempts "
"to reuse an existing Chrome tab via AppleScript.<br> Otherwise, falls "
"back to [opn](https://github.com/sindresorhus/opn) behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:314
msgid ""
"`printHostingInstructions(appPackage: Object, publicUrl: string, "
"publicPath: string, buildFolder: string, useYarn: boolean): void`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:316
msgid "Prints hosting instructions after the project is built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:318
msgid ""
"Pass your parsed `package.json` object as `appPackage`, your URL where "
"you plan to host the app as `publicUrl`, `output.publicPath` from your "
"webpack configuration as `publicPath`, the `buildFolder` name, and "
"whether to `useYarn` in instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:327
msgid "`WebpackDevServerUtils`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:329
msgid "`choosePort(host: string, defaultPort: number): Promise<number | null>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:331
msgid ""
"Returns a Promise resolving to either `defaultPort` or next available "
"port if the user confirms it is okay to do. If the port is taken and the "
"user has refused to use another port, or if the terminal is not "
"interactive and can’t present user with the choice, resolves to `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:333
msgid "`createCompiler(args: Object): WebpackCompiler`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:335
msgid ""
"Creates a webpack compiler instance for WebpackDevServer with built-in "
"helpful messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:337
msgid "The `args` object accepts a number of properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:339
msgid "**appName** `string`: The name that will be printed to the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:340
msgid ""
"**config** `Object`: The webpack configuration options to be provided to "
"the webpack constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:341
msgid ""
"**devSocket** `Object`: Required if `useTypeScript` is `true`. This "
"object should include `errors` and `warnings` which are functions "
"accepting an array of errors or warnings emitted by the type checking. "
"This is useful when running `fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin` with `async:"
" true` to report errors that are emitted after the webpack build is "
"complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:342
msgid ""
"**urls** `Object`: To provide the `urls` argument, use `prepareUrls()` "
"described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:343
msgid ""
"**useYarn** `boolean`: If `true`, yarn instructions will be emitted in "
"the terminal instead of npm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:344
msgid ""
"**useTypeScript** `boolean`: If `true`, TypeScript type checking will be "
"enabled. Be sure to provide the `devSocket` argument above if this is set"
" to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:345
msgid ""
"**tscCompileOnError** `boolean`: If `true`, errors in TypeScript type "
"checking will not prevent start script from running app, and will not "
"cause build script to exit unsuccessfully. Also downgrades all TypeScript"
" type checking error messages to warning messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:346
msgid "**webpack** `function`: A reference to the webpack constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:348
msgid ""
"`prepareProxy(proxySetting: string, appPublicFolder: string, "
"servedPathname: string): Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:350
msgid ""
"Creates a WebpackDevServer `proxy` configuration object from the `proxy` "
"setting in `package.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:352
msgid ""
"`prepareUrls(protocol: string, host: string, port: number, pathname: "
"string = '/'): Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:354
msgid ""
"Returns an object with local and remote URLs for the development server. "
"Pass this object to `createCompiler()` described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:356
msgid "`webpackHotDevClient`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:358
msgid ""
"This is an alternative client for "
"[WebpackDevServer](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server) that "
"shows a syntax error overlay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:360
msgid "It currently supports only webpack 3.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:378
msgid ""
"`getCSSModuleLocalIdent(context: Object, localIdentName: String, "
"localName: String, options: Object): string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:380
msgid ""
"Creates a class name for CSS Modules that uses either the filename or "
"folder name if named `index.module.css`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:382
msgid ""
"For `MyFolder/MyComponent.module.css` and class `MyClass` the output will"
" be `MyComponent.module_MyClass__[hash]` For `MyFolder/index.module.css` "
"and class `MyClass` the output will be `MyFolder_MyClass__[hash]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:415
msgid "`getCacheIdentifier(environment: string, packages: string[]): string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/react-dev-utils_README.md:417
msgid ""
"Returns a cache identifier (string) consisting of the specified "
"environment and related package versions, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

